/**
 * @file http_server.h
 * @brief HTTP endpoints (FROZEN CONTRACT V1.5 §5, Sprint P2; V1.6.4/V1.6.5 Sprint D1). Runs in the network task (Core 0).
 *
 * Library: WebServer (Arduino core). All handlers return quickly.
 *   GET  /            -> SPIFFS /www/index.html
 *   GET  /settings    -> SPIFFS /www/settings.html
 *   GET  /add         -> SPIFFS /add.json  (application/json, Cache-Control: no-store)
 *   GET  /add.html    -> SPIFFS /add.html (V1.6.5: a file generated by scripts/build_data.py, ADD spec §5.3)
 *   GET  /llms.txt    -> generated index (ADD spec §5.4)
 *   GET  /openapi.json -> SPIFFS /openapi.json (application/json, Cache-Control: no-store)   V1.6.4
 *   GET  /doc         -> SPIFFS /doc.html (text/html)   V1.5.27, was /doc.md (text/markdown)
 *   V1.5.22 (web UI assets, Sprint W1):
 *   GET  /app.js      -> SPIFFS /www/app.js (application/javascript)
 *   GET  /style.css   -> SPIFFS /www/style.css (text/css)
 *   GET  /font-u400.woff2, /font-u700.woff2, /font-m400.woff2, /font-m700.woff2 -> SPIFFS /www/<same name>
 *        (font/woff2, Cache-Control: max-age=86400; SPIFFS names are limited to 31 characters)
 *   GET  /favicon.ico -> SPIFFS /www/favicon.ico (image/x-icon, Cache-Control: max-age=86400)   V1.6.5
 *   GET  /log         -> logDump() (text/plain)
 *   GET  /proc        -> snapshotGet() + procToJson() (Cache-Control: no-store)
 *   POST /api         -> body max API_BODY_MAX bytes, then:
 *        1. apiParseRequest(); error -> response with that error (HTTP 400 for BAD_CRC/BAD_JSON, else 200)
 *        2. valid packet (CRC ok, known cmd) -> snapshotSetLastApiRx(millis())
 *        3. GET_STATE  -> reply locally: extra = stateExtraToJson(snapshot.state, snapshot.err,
 *                          snapshot.local, CycleStats from snapshotGetCycleStats())   (V1.1)
 *           GET_CONFIG -> reply locally: extra = paramsToJsonMember(snapshotGetConfig())
 *           others     -> cmdQueueSendAndWait(cmd, API_REPLY_TIMEOUT_MS)
 *        4. responseToJson(); Content-Type application/json; HTTP 200
 *           (also for LOCAL_CONTROL = -10: the device is fine, the operator has priority)
 *   Every response: Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *  (dashboards on other hosts)
 *   Unknown path -> 404 {"error":"not found"}
 *
 * V1.5.16 – exact behaviour (tested natively with WebServer/SPIFFS shims: test/native/test_http_server):
 *  - One file-static WebServer server(HTTP_PORT). httpServerInit registers every route with
 *    server.on(path, method, handler) and server.onNotFound(), then server.begin().
 *    httpServerLoop() only calls server.handleClient().
 *  - Every response first sends the header Access-Control-Allow-Origin: * (server.sendHeader).
 *  - OPTIONS /api (CORS preflight of browsers on other hosts): 204, empty body, headers
 *    Access-Control-Allow-Methods: GET, POST, OPTIONS and Access-Control-Allow-Headers: Content-Type.
 *  - Files (V1.6.5: gzip copies): one helper for every file route except the fonts:
 *      static void sendFile(const char* path, const char* type, const char* cache, bool pragma = false)
 *    cache = value of Cache-Control or nullptr (no header); pragma = also send Pragma: no-cache.
 *    1. useGz = the request header Accept-Encoding contains "gzip" (server.header("Accept-Encoding")
 *       .indexOf("gzip") >= 0) AND SPIFFS.exists(path + ".gz").
 *    2. If !useGz and !SPIFFS.exists(path) -> the 404 answer (and nothing else: no further headers).
 *    3. Open path + ".gz" if useGz, else path. Headers in this order: Cache-Control (if cache),
 *       Pragma: no-cache (if pragma), Vary: Accept-Encoding (always), then cors().
 *       server.streamFile(f, type); f.close().
 *    Do NOT send Content-Encoding yourself: WebServer::streamFile adds "Content-Encoding: gzip" by
 *    itself for a file whose name ends in ".gz" (ESP32 core 3.x, also in the test shim). The type stays
 *    the type of the content (e.g. text/html), never application/x-gzip.
 *    httpServerInit() calls server.collectHeaders(keys, 1) with keys = {"Accept-Encoding"} BEFORE
 *    server.begin() – the WebServer keeps only collected request headers, header() is "" otherwise.
 *    Until V1.6.4: if SPIFFS.exists(path): File f = SPIFFS.open(path, "r"); server.streamFile(f, type);
 *    f.close(). Missing file -> the 404 answer. Types: "/" and "/settings" text/html,
 *    "/add" application/json (+ Cache-Control: no-store), "/doc" text/html (V1.5.27),
 *    "/openapi.json" application/json (+ Cache-Control: no-store) (V1.6.4, Sprint D1).
 *  - /add.html (V1.6.5): sendFile("/add.html", "text/html; charset=utf-8",
 *    "no-store, no-cache, must-revalidate", true)  – the headers of ADD spec §5.3. The page is the file
 *    data/add.html (generated from add.json by scripts/build_data.py, checked by test/js/test_add.js);
 *    the runtime generation of V1.5.16/V1.5.17 (64-byte chunks, about 24 s for 34 kB on the device)
 *    and its helpers are removed.
 *    Calls: "/" -> ("/www/index.html", "text/html", nullptr), "/settings" -> ("/www/settings.html",
 *    "text/html", nullptr), "/add" -> ("/add.json", "application/json", "no-store"), "/openapi.json" ->
 *    ("/openapi.json", "application/json", "no-store"), "/doc" -> ("/doc.html", "text/html", nullptr),
 *    "/app.js" -> ("/www/app.js", "application/javascript", nullptr), "/style.css" -> ("/www/style.css",
 *    "text/css", nullptr).
 *  - Fonts and favicon (V1.6.5): the font helper becomes
 *      static void sendCached(const char* path, const char* type)
 *    (as before: missing -> 404; Cache-Control: max-age=86400, cors(), streamFile(f, type); no .gz lookup).
 *    Fonts: sendCached("/www/font-<name>.woff2", "font/woff2"); new route
 *    "/favicon.ico" -> sendCached("/www/favicon.ico", "image/x-icon").
 *  - /llms.txt: text/plain, exactly these 5 lines (V1.6.4: line 4 new), each ending with '\n':
 *      # AI Device Description (ADD)
 *      - ADD (JSON): [Device Description](/add)
 *      - ADD (HTML): [Device Description for Cloud-AI](/add.html)
 *      - OpenAPI (JSON): [HTTP API, technical reference](/openapi.json)
 *      - Documentation: [Device manual](/doc)
 *  - /log: text/plain, logDump() into a static buffer of LOG_LINES * LOG_LINE_LEN + 1 bytes.
 *  - /proc: snapshotGet + procToJson into char[PROC_JSON_MAX]; application/json, Cache-Control: no-store.
 *  - POST /api: body = server.arg("plain"). No body or length > API_BODY_MAX -> BAD_JSON.
 *    Otherwise apiParseRequest(body, length, cmd). Packet is "valid" if the result is OK or
 *    BAD_PARAM (CRC ok, known cmd) -> snapshotSetLastApiRx(millis()). Every error (V1.5.17: also BAD_PARAM
 *    for GET_STATE / GET_CONFIG) -> responseToJson
 *    (cmd.id, err, nullptr, nullptr, ...) with HTTP 400 for BAD_CRC/BAD_JSON, else 200.
 *    OK: GET_STATE / GET_CONFIG answered locally (extra as listed above, ProcData from
 *    snapshotGet), all other commands: err = cmdQueueSendAndWait(cmd, API_REPLY_TIMEOUT_MS),
 *    response responseToJson(cmd.id, err, nullptr, nullptr, ...), HTTP 200.
 *    Response buffer: static char[1024]; Content-Type application/json.
 *  - 404 answer: HTTP 404, application/json, body {"error":"not found"}.
 *
 * V1.5.25: the server is an AddWebServer (subclass of WebServer). httpServerLoop() first closes a
 *  connection that has sent no request for HTTP_IDLE_DROP_MS (browser spare connections blocked
 *  every other client for up to 5 s), then calls handleClient(). /log: "http: idle connection
 *  closed after 500 ms (<n> so far)", at most one line per HTTP_IDLE_LOG_MS.
 */
#pragma once

void httpServerInit();   ///< mounts nothing; SPIFFS is mounted in setup()
void httpServerLoop();   ///< server.handleClient()
